Shortened programming words (num[ber], param[eter], str[ing], etc.) have
large negative responses; full spellings and initialisms such as URL do not
match. A clipping embedded in a continuing word has half the response.
Related rules cover Latin/Greek stems, Romance prepositions, tool markers,
escaped quotes and indentation around 20-35 columns. Standalone carriage
returns, nonbreaking spaces, dash runs and damaged Unicode get separate
negative responses. Remaining tokens use small length/script baselines.

